(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the grammatical pathology of sentence fragments and demonstrate three systematic remediation techniques in technical reports.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Grammatical Pathology of Fragments:) Tj
T*
(   A sentence fragment is an incomplete grammatical construction punctuated as if it were a) Tj
T*
(   complete sentence. Fragments typically lack a finite verb, lack an explicit syntactic subject,) Tj
T*
(   or represent an unattached dependent clause:) Tj
T*
(   - Dependent Clause Fragment: "Because the autoclave failed to maintain 121 deg C for 15) Tj
T*
(   minutes.") Tj
T*
(   - Participial Phrase Fragment: "Resulting in extensive bacterial contamination of the nutrient) Tj
T*
(   agar.") Tj
T*
(   - Appositive Fragment: "Especially Taq polymerase, Pfu polymerase, and reverse transcriptase.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Systematic Remediation Techniques:) Tj
T*
(   - Method 1 \(Syntactic Attachment to Adjacent Matrix Clause\):) Tj
T*
(   - Combine the subordinate fragment with the preceding or following independent clause:) Tj
T*
(   - "Because the autoclave failed to maintain 121 deg C for 15 minutes, the nutrient agar) Tj
T*
(   suffered extensive bacterial contamination.") Tj
T*
(   - Method 2 \(Supply Missing Subject and Finite Verb\):) Tj
T*
(   - Transform the non-finite phrase into an independent clause:) Tj
T*
(   - "This equipment malfunction resulted in extensive bacterial contamination of the nutrient) Tj
T*
(   agar.") Tj
T*
(   - Method 3 \(Nominal Integration\):) Tj
T*
(   - "The laboratory stocked several essential enzymes, especially Taq polymerase, Pfu polymerase,) Tj
T*
(   and reverse transcriptase.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze comma splices and fused sentences in academic prose, detailing four grammatically sound correction methods.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definitions of Comma Splices and Fused Sentences:) Tj
T*
(   - Comma Splice: Two independent clauses joined with only a comma without an accompanying) Tj
T*
(   coordinating conjunction:) Tj
T*
(   - Error: "The wild-type cells grew rapidly, the mutant strain failed to divide.") Tj
T*
(   - Fused \(Run-on\) Sentence: Two independent clauses joined with no punctuation mark whatsoever:) Tj
T*
(   - Error: "The wild-type cells grew rapidly the mutant strain failed to divide.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Four Grammatically Sound Correction Strategies:) Tj
T*
(   - Strategy 1 \(Period / Full Stop\): Divide into two discrete sentences:) Tj
T*
(   - "The wild-type cells grew rapidly. The mutant strain failed to divide.") Tj
T*
(   - Strategy 2 \(Semicolon\): Join closely related independent propositions:) Tj
T*
(   - "The wild-type cells grew rapidly; the mutant strain failed to divide.") Tj
T*
(   - Strategy 3 \(Comma + FANBOYS Coordinating Conjunction\):) Tj
T*
(   - "The wild-type cells grew rapidly, but the mutant strain failed to divide.") Tj
T*
(   - Strategy 4 \(Subordination\): Subordinate one clause to create a complex sentence:) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
