/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the syntax of misplaced, dangling, and squinting modifiers in laboratory protocols, providing unambiguous revisions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Taxonomy of Modifying Errors:) Tj
T*
(   - Misplaced Modifiers: Separated too far from the word they modify, creating unintentional) Tj
T*
(   absurdity:) Tj
T*
(   - Flawed: "The technician observed a dividing bacterium with a damaged ocular lens." \(Implies) Tj
T*
(   the bacterium has a lens\).) Tj
T*
(   - Revision: "Using a damaged ocular lens, the technician observed a dividing bacterium.") Tj
T*
(   - Dangling Modifiers: An introductory participial or prepositional phrase whose logical agent) Tj
T*
(   is missing from the main clause:) Tj
T*
(   - Flawed: "After centrifuging the lysate at 14,000 rpm, the supernatant was discarded." \(The) Tj
T*
(   supernatant did not centrifuge itself\).) Tj
T*
(   - Revision: "After centrifuging the lysate at 14,000 rpm, the researcher discarded the) Tj
T*
(   supernatant.") Tj
T*
(   - Squinting \(Two-Way\) Modifiers: An adverb sandwiched between two syntactic elements, making it) Tj
T*
(   ambiguous which one it modifies:) Tj
T*
(   - Flawed: "Patients who exercise regularly experience fewer inflammatory episodes." \(Does) Tj
T*
(   'regularly' modify exercise or experience?\).) Tj
T*
(   - Revision A: "Patients who regularly exercise experience fewer inflammatory episodes.") Tj
T*
(   - Revision B: "Patients who exercise experience fewer inflammatory episodes on a regular) Tj
T*
(   basis.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 6:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the principle of grammatical and syntactic parallelism in research article methodologies, results, and headings.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Principle of Parallelism:) Tj
T*
(   Syntactic parallelism requires that coordinate grammatical elements \(items in a series,) Tj
T*
(   comparative elements, or pairs joined by correlative conjunctions\) share identical grammatical) Tj
T*
(   form \(e.g., all gerunds, all imperative verbs, all prepositional phrases, all noun phrases\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Methodology and List Parallelism:) Tj
T*
(   - Non-Parallel Protocol:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Thawing the frozen cell stock at 37 deg C. \(Gerund phrase\)) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Transfer 1 mL to a sterile centrifuge tube. \(Imperative verb\)) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: Centrifugation for 5 minutes at 1,000 g. \(Noun phrase\)) Tj
T*
(   - Fully Parallel Protocol \(All Imperative Verbs\):) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Thaw the frozen cell stock at 37 deg C.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Transfer 1 mL to a sterile centrifuge tube.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: Centrifuge the suspension for 5 minutes at 1,000 g.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Correlative Conjunction Parallelism:) Tj
T*
(   - Non-Parallel: "The drug was evaluated both for its cytotoxicity and how stable it was.") Tj
T*
(   - Parallel: "The drug was evaluated both for its cytotoxicity and for its stability.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 7:) Tj
T*
