(   2. Core Syntactic Rules:) Tj
T*
(   - Polarity Reversal:) Tj
T*
(   - Positive Declarative Stem -> Negative Tag:) Tj
T*
(   - "The autoclave reached operating temperature, didn't it?") Tj
T*
(   - Negative Declarative Stem -> Positive Tag:) Tj
T*
(   - "The reagent has not expired, has it?") Tj
T*
(   - Auxiliary Matching: The tag must reproduce the exact auxiliary or modal verb present in the) Tj
T*
(   stem:) Tj
T*
(   - "The biosensor can detect femtomolar concentrations, can't it?") Tj
T*
(   - 'Do'-Support: When the stem contains an ordinary lexical verb without an auxiliary, use) Tj
T*
(   do/does/did:) Tj
T*
(   - "The bacteria synthesize flagella under starvation, don't they?") Tj
T*
(   - Pronoun Subject: The tag subject must always be a personal pronoun matching the stem subject.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Special Idiomatic Cases:) Tj
T*
(   - Stem with 'I am': Tag is 'aren't I?' \(or 'am I not?' in hyper-formal registers\): "I am next) Tj
T*
(   to defend the thesis, aren't I?") Tj
T*
(   - Imperative Proposals with 'Let's': Tag is 'shall we?': "Let's review the gel electrophoresis) Tj
T*
(   data, shall we?") Tj
T*
(   - Negative Indefinite Subjects \(nobody, nothing, neither\): Stem is negative, so tag must be) Tj
T*
(   positive: "Nothing contaminated the sterile hood, did it?") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
