(   2. Syntactic Variants:) Tj
T*
(   - 'It'-Cleft: Structure: It + [form of be] + [focused constituent] + [that/who clause]:) Tj
T*
(   - Canonical: "Enzymatic cleavage at site A prevented viral entry.") Tj
T*
(   - Cleft: "It was enzymatic cleavage at site A that prevented viral entry.") Tj
T*
(   - Function: Directly refutes competing hypotheses \(e.g., proving that cleavage at site A, not) Tj
T*
(   site B, was the causative factor\).) Tj
T*
(   - 'Wh'-Cleft \(Pseudo-Cleft\): Structure: [Wh-clause] + [form of be] + [focused element]:) Tj
T*
(   - "What surprised the investigators was the extraordinary stability of the hyperthermophilic) Tj
T*
(   enzyme.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Concord in 'It'-Clefts:) Tj
T*
(   The relative clause verb in an 'it'-cleft agrees with the focused constituent, not with the) Tj
T*
(   dummy pronoun 'it':) Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "It is the altered post-translational modifications that are responsible for poor) Tj
T*
(   receptor binding.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
