(>> Solution to Question 16:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the syntax of correlative conjunctions and analyze errors in parallel structures involving scientific comparisons.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Correlative Structural Balance:) Tj
T*
(   Correlative conjunctions work in tandem to establish balanced coordinate comparisons:) Tj
T*
(   - Pairs: not only...but also; either...or; neither...nor; both...and; whether...or.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Structural Parallelism Law:) Tj
T*
(   Both arms of the correlative pair must govern syntactically equivalent constituents:) Tj
T*
(   - If the first element is followed by an infinitive phrase, the second must be an infinitive) Tj
T*
(   phrase.) Tj
T*
(   - If followed by a prepositional phrase, the second must be a prepositional phrase.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Diagnostic Error and Correction in Biomedical Context:) Tj
T*
(   - Flawed: "The researchers sought not only to isolate the antibiotic [infinitive phrase] but) Tj
T*
(   also analyzed its chemical structure [past tense verb phrase].") Tj
T*
(   - Correction A: "The researchers sought not only to isolate the antibiotic but also to analyze) Tj
T*
(   its chemical structure." \(Parallel infinitives\).) Tj
T*
(   - Correction B: "The researchers not only isolated the antibiotic but also analyzed its) Tj
T*
(   chemical structure." \(Parallel past-tense predicates\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 17:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the syntax and punctuation of appositive phrases in defining technical terms and novel biotechnology reagents.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Apposition Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   An appositive is a nominal constituent that renames, specifies, or defines an immediately) Tj
T*
(   preceding noun phrase. It can be a single noun, a phrase, or a clause.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Restrictive vs. Non-Restrictive Appositives:) Tj
T*
(   - Non-Restrictive \(Parenthetical Definition\):) Tj
T*
(   - Adds explanatory information about an entity already uniquely identified; set off by commas:) Tj
T*
(   - "Taq polymerase, a thermostable enzyme isolated from Thermus aquaticus, revolutionized PCR) Tj
T*
(   amplification.") Tj
T*
(   - Restrictive \(Essential Identifier\):) Tj
T*
