(>> Solution to Question 29:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the syntactic criteria for forming grammatically valid compound-complex sentences in academic literature.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Anatomy:) Tj
T*
(   A compound-complex sentence combines at least two coordinate independent clauses \(joined by a) Tj
T*
(   coordinating conjunction or semicolon\) with at least one subordinate dependent clause.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Syntactic Criteria for Validity:) Tj
T*
(   - Complete Clause Integrity: Each independent clause must possess its own subject and finite) Tj
T*
(   verb.) Tj
T*
(   - Subordination Accuracy: Dependent clauses must be clearly introduced by appropriate) Tj
T*
(   subordinating conjunctions or relative pronouns.) Tj
T*
(   - Hierarchy of Punctuation: Commas separate introductory dependent clauses and coordinate) Tj
T*
(   independent clauses; semicolons separate independent clauses when internal commas exist.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Exemplary Syntactic Construction in Biotechnology:) Tj
T*
(   - Clause 1 \(Subordinate\): "Although the wild-type plasmid replicated efficiently at 37 deg C,") Tj
T*
(   - Clause 2 \(Independent\): "the temperature-sensitive mutant failed to initiate DNA synthesis,") Tj
T*
(   - Clause 3 \(Independent\): "and subsequent gel electrophoresis confirmed the absence of plasmid) Tj
T*
(   bands.") Tj
T*
(   - Full Sentence: "Although the wild-type plasmid replicated efficiently at 37 deg C, the) Tj
T*
(   temperature-sensitive mutant failed to initiate DNA synthesis, and subsequent gel) Tj
T*
(   electrophoresis confirmed the absence of plasmid bands.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 30:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine common syntactic errors in question-tag formations involving indefinite pronouns and semi-negative adverbs.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Tag Concord with Indefinite Person Pronouns:) Tj
T*
(   Indefinite pronouns denoting persons \(everyone, everybody, someone, somebody, no one, nobody,) Tj
T*
(   anyone, anybody\) take singular verbs in their main clause, but take the plural personal pronoun) Tj
T*
(   'they' in the question tag. Consequently, the tag verb must be plural:) Tj
T*
(   - Stem: "Everyone completed the safety training." \(Completed is past\).) Tj
T*
(   - Tag: "...didn't they?" \(Not *didn't he?\).) Tj
T*
(   - Stem: "Nobody has entered the cleanroom." \(Present perfect\).) Tj
T*
(   - Tag: "...have they?" \(Not *has he? or *has they?\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Semi-Negative Adverbial Stems:) Tj
T*
(   When a stem contains an inherently negative or semi-negative adverb \(scarcely, rarely, barely,) Tj
T*
(   seldom, hardly\), the stem is grammatically negative. Therefore, the tag must be positive:) Tj
T*
(   - Incorrect: "The culture rarely exhibits contamination, doesn't it?") Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "The culture rarely exhibits contamination, does it?") Tj
T*
(   - Incorrect: "The thermal sensor barely detected the exotherm, didn't it?") Tj
T*
ET

